TY  - JOUR
TI  - The Reflection Principle and the Ex-Ante Pareto Principle in Anna Mahtani’s <i>Objects of Credence</i>
AU  - Bovens, Luc
PY  - 2024
T2  - Economics and Philosophy
AB  - First, Mahtani argues that both in the game The Mug and in the Sleeping Beauty we should not defer to a trusted person under a particular designation if they do not self-identify under this designation. This invites a more complex Reflection Principle. I respond that there are more parsimonious ways to avoid the challenges posed to the Reflection Principle. Second, Mahtani argues that preferences create a hyperintensional context, which poses a challenge to the Ex-Ante Pareto Principle that can be averted by supervaluation. I respond that such an appeal to supervaluation would block randomization as a fair allocation device.
